{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>By lot.</b> After they divided into twelve territories." "<b>Heritage shall be divided.</b> Each tribe, by lot, according to the number of heads of families in it — for example, four for Reuven, five for Shimon, and so for all of them." "<b>Between the many and the few.</b> How so? Four families for Reuven: two large and two small. One of the large ones divides its land into three parts by means of lots and tickets: two parts for two large families, and the third part goes back and is divided into two for the two small families. And so for all the remaining tribes, until all the portions are divided by lot — all fifty-seven portions for fifty-seven families. <b>Between the many and the few</b> — the lamed has a dot in chirik (i.e., it is written with a cholam vowel dot, namely לֹ)."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {2 "The Hebrew למ״ד נקודה בחיר״ק is obscure; I translate hyper-literally. The phrase seems to describe an irregular vowel pointing on the lamed of למעט, but its precise technical meaning is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:56.729006314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}